  "description": "ZOKBUZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C136 H104 Gd4 N12 O16,2(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.579-3.910 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.92-111.46°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C140H110Gd4N14O16.",
